internal/form/sizes.go was listed here until 2026-09-08, against both
ui/overlay/textInput_size.go and ui/overlay/textInput_render.go. Neither
half held any longer. The size half -- atrium's shared height budget and
its drop-lines degradation cascade -- was deleted with the v1 compose path
and nothing derived from it survives anywhere. The render half is PaintLine,
whose body moved to internal/form/widgets/paint.go, leaving sizes.go with a
one-line delegator, two layout constants the file's own header calls this
form's own, and boldSpan. So the entry named a file that no longer carried
the code while the file that did carry it went unlisted.

The attribution moved with the code rather than being dropped: whether
PaintLine is a port or an independent re-implementation of the same guard is
genuinely arguable from its own doc comments, and the conservative answer to
an arguable case is to keep the credit and put it where the code is.

atrium's ui/overlay/textInput.go and ui/overlay/branchPicker.go are not on
the clean list (each carries surviving third-party lines from other atrium
contributors) and were never opened as porting sources. Two files in this
repository provide equivalent functionality as independent reimplementations
instead of ports: internal/form/widgets/textarea.go (prompt/title text
widget, built directly against charm.land/bubbles/v2's textarea) and
internal/form/field_worktree.go (worktree base-ref picker, built on this
repository's own widgets.Picker). Every other file in this repository is
original work.

